The full-pipeline permutation test handles labels that vary within a subject: `ChanceAssessmentConfig(permutation_scheme="within_strata", strata_column="Subject")` shuffles sample labels inside each stratum, keeping its class counts. `permutation_scheme="blocks_within_strata"` with `block_column="Run"` shuffles the labels of single-label blocks between the blocks of each stratum. The default `"units"` scheme is unchanged. The result metadata, the row assumptions and the report state what was permuted. `ChanceAssessmentConfig(method="sign_flip")` adds a group-level test for leave-one-group-out CV: per-subject fold scores minus chance are sign-flipped across subjects and ranked by their one-sample t, with t-max over time and no refits. `permute_labels_within_strata` draws one stratified permutation on its own.
